    {
      "id": "eRL7YR3Mi4md6FI9yxGux",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 270.6711033166377,
      "y": 7710.041189609066,
      "width": 774.839111328125,
      "height": 350,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bAS",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 687136879,
      "version": 653,
      "versionNonce": 699942671,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1743893322377,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "* Model:\n - Unconditional diffusion model that generates faces\n - Loaded from HF: https://huggingface.co/google/ddpm-celebahq-256\n - Trained on CelebA-HQ (30K 256x256 images of celebrities)\n    . https://www.tensorflow.org/datasets/catalog/celeb_a_hq#celeb_a_hq256\n\n* Reward:\n  - Score of a classification model that classifies men vs women\n  - Loaded from HF: https://huggingface.co/rizvandwiki/gender-classification\n\n* RL algorithm:\n  - GRPO\n  - Different KL implementation (probably)\n  - Optionally adding gradient clipping",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "* Model:\n - Unconditional diffusion model that generates faces\n - Loaded from HF: https://huggingface.co/google/ddpm-celebahq-256\n - Trained on CelebA-HQ (30K 256x256 images of celebrities)\n    . https://www.tensorflow.org/datasets/catalog/celeb_a_hq#celeb_a_hq256\n\n* Reward:\n  - Score of a classification model that classifies men vs women\n  - Loaded from HF: https://huggingface.co/rizvandwiki/gender-classification\n\n* RL algorithm:\n  - GRPO\n  - Different KL implementation (probably)\n  - Optionally adding gradient clipping",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "XhGGqe6aYH44bBvH1TbTG",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1213.136611565708,
      "y": 7724.906912000411,
      "width": 826.8527425130209,
      "height": 425,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bAT",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2103810799,
      "version": 1639,
      "versionNonce": 598782735,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1743893712762,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "* Need to study advantage estimation better\n  - What if I could implment something like a discount factor?\n  - It doesn't seem to me that every step should contribute equally\n  - If I have a trajectory of a woman, maybe I don't want to discourage\n    the whole trajectory, only the later steps\n\n* GRPO uses a specific KL divergence equation, need to review that                    \n\n* Men and women are oscilating \"in phase\", even though, on average, men\n  increase their probability and women decrease\n\n* When training for various epochs without resampling, only the early steps\n  contribute to the optimization\n\n*DDPM is the most basic form of sampling, I still need to explore\n  DDIM and others\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "* Need to study advantage estimation better\n  - What if I could implment something like a discount factor?\n  - It doesn't seem to me that every step should contribute equally\n  - If I have a trajectory of a woman, maybe I don't want to discourage\n    the whole trajectory, only the later steps\n\n* GRPO uses a specific KL divergence equation, need to review that                                                                                                                                             \n\n* Men and women are oscilating \"in phase\", even though, on average, men\n  increase their probability and women decrease\n\n* When training for various epochs without resampling, only the early steps\n  contribute to the optimization\n\n*DDPM is the most basic form of sampling, I still need to explore\n  DDIM and others\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
